t they said there will be a  war but i watched the news and  lukashenka said there won't be a war  they brought some tanks and trucks we  thought there was a war but it turned  out it was a test of military readiness  vladimir katsura the leader of an  opposition party in holmel is not that  optimistic he says many people in  belarus would like to demonstrate  against a possible war but are too  scared to do so  i'm personally very worried i have  family i don't want war like most  belarusians but as i see the  developments going on so far under the  disguise of military exercises it  naturally makes me very worried  on this main road to ukraine's capital  kiev buses and trucks are still crossing  the border but kiev is only 200  kilometers away and russia's show of  military force nearby is making people  in ukraine and western powers very  nervous staff farsan al jazeera in  subrovka belarus
 

